{title: At Your Name (Yahweh Yahweh)}
{artist: Phil Wickham}
{key: G}

{comment: Verse 1}
At Your [G]Name, the mountains shake and [C]crumble
At Your [G]Name, the oceans roar and [C]tumble
At Your [D]Name, angels will [Em]bow the earth will
[C]rejoice
Your people cry [D]out

{comment: Chorus}
[Gsus]Lord of all [G]the earth
We shout Your Name, shout Your Name
[Em]Filling up the skies
With endless praise, endless praise
[D]Yahweh, Yahweh
We [C]love to shout Your Name
Oh [G]Lord

{comment: Verse 2}
At Your [G]Name, the morning breaks in [C]glory
At Your [G]Name, creation sings Your [C]story
At Your [D]Name, angles will bow [Em]the earth will [C]rejoice
Your people cry [D]out

{comment: Bridge}
There is [D]no one like our God
We will [Em]praise You, [C]praise You
[D]There is no one like our God
We will [G]sing, we will sing!

{comment: Bridge 2}
There is [D]no one like our God
We will [Em]praise You, [C]praise You
[D]Jesus You are God
We will [C]sing!  [D]   [Em]   [D]

